**Issue**: #418
**Date**: 2026-09-23
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

Feature: Recover an approved-spec start and pre-publication implementation
  Only exact owner-bound evidence permits a single normal worker recovery.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Worktree releases old issue branch after failed checkout
    Given start failed with branch_checkout_failed at a clean exact default checkpoint and another worktree owns the issue branch
    When that worktree releases the branch and discovery proves the unique run owner, strict handoff and absent worker
    Then one start recovery archives the failed handoff and dispatches the normal worker
    And unchanged ownership or consumed recovery remains blocked

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Squash-merged approved spec has divergent old branch
    Given approved spec-only PR history is on default but the old issue branch is not its ancestor
    When start proves source and merges approved default without rewriting the old branch
    Then exact merge history and in-scope tree are proven and the branch is synchronized upstream without force
    And its passed handoff records the actual branch and head

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Start advances the controller before implementation
    Given start passed on an exact synchronized issue head different from its default checkpoint
    When execute accepts that handoff
    Then it atomically records the issue branch head before implement dispatch
    And a stale, unpushed or mismatched head blocks dispatch

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Preserved dirty implementation after pre-publication rejection
    Given two exact pre-existing reconciliation commits are now synchronized and no implementation commit exists
    And the unique owner preserved nonempty authorized dirty implementation and a failed handoff
    When discovery reproves the scope and consumes one recovery
    Then the normal implement worker binds, commits, pushes and hands off the preserved work
    And a second consumption cannot replay the dispatch

  @SCN005 @safety
  Scenario: Ambiguous source or ownership preserves evidence
    Given a changed head, conflicting worktree, different PR, ambiguous owner, non-exact history or denied dirty path
    When recovery is inspected
    Then checkpoint, handoff and evidence remain unchanged
    And no force push, branch takeover or worker dispatch occurs

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: A changeable start or implement blocker reports its proof and one action
    Given START is blocked by an identified other worktree or IMPLEMENT by an exact unsynchronized reconciliation head
    When the controller stops
    Then its output names the observed branch/head or owner and the failed proof
    And it offers only a bounded owner-safe release or non-force synchronization action
    When that external fact changes and discovery re-probes once
    Then the same issue resumes automatically through the normal worker if exact authority is proven

  @SCN007 @safety
  Scenario: Ambiguous or consumed recovery reports the missing proof without replay
    Given the branch owner, source PR, head, dirty scope or prior dispatch is ambiguous or consumed
    When recovery is classified or the controller stops
    Then the output identifies the missing proof and preserves checkpoint and handoff
    And it does not prompt for an unsafe replay, force push, worktree takeover or provider bypass

  @SCN008 @acceptance
  Scenario: Same retained PennyScan issue proves merged recovery end to end
    Given PennyScan issue 217 retains its failed implement checkpoint and preserved dirty work
    When candidate discovery runs read-only from the exact PennyScan root
    Then the classifier reports an exact recovery or named missing proof without mutating evidence
    When the #418 PR and a separate registered smoke pass and the clean merged plugin is pinned
    Then the existing Herdr OMP controller resumes issue 217 through a new exact-head merged implementation PR and closed issue
    And issue 218 is not attempted first
